<title>USA: Manatron to buy back 100,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Manatron to buy back 100,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>KALAMAZOO, Mich. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manatron Inc said Thursday it had authorized the buyback of 100,000 shares in open-market transactions over the next 11 months, contingent on market conditions.</p>
<p>Manatron also said it had approved a preferred stock purchase rights plan, under which holders could buy a new series of preferred stock in the event of a hostile takeover attempt. The rights would be distributed to shareholders of record June 16, the company said.</p>
<p>The rights would be triggered if a person or group buys 15 percent or more of the company's common stock.</p>
</text>
